---
/**
 * Our perspective. The emotional core of the page: name the reader's
 * suspicion of meditation culture, flip it, and make the renunciative vs
 * life-affirming contrast concrete. The Jared quote is a cofounder's
 * confession, not a testimonial.
 */
---

<section class="stance-section grain" id="approach" aria-labelledby="stance-heading">
	<div class="sheet">
		<span class="label-caps sheet-margin">Our perspective</span>

		<h2 id="stance-heading" class="stance-heading">
			Most meditation systems are trying to fix you. They suggest you are fundamentally broken.
		</h2>

		<div class="stance-prose">
			<p>
				There is nothing fundamentally wrong with you. A lot of meditation is renunciative: emotions
				are noise, thoughts are failures, ordinary life is the thing you retreat from. This practice
				runs the other way. We train richer involvement in our ordinary life, not a graceful calm
				exit from it.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can remain connected and present in any circumstance, however frightening or exciting it
				seems. You develop the capacity to hold the intensity, the joy, and the ordinary textures of
				existence with spacious clarity.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="stance-collation sheet-wide">
			<div class="stance-col stance-col--this">
				<h3 class="label-caps">This practice</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Emotions are welcome. All of them.</li>
					<li>No sound is distracting, no thought is bad, no experience is wrong.</li>
					<li>Clarity with connection to people, work, and circumstances.</li>
					<li>Ordinary life is the arena. More of life, not less.</li>
					<li>Encourages being effective without striving.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="stance-col">
				<h3 class="label-caps">The renunciate habit</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>One more exhausting, effort-based self-improvement project.</li>
					<li>Emotions are obstacles to be managed and controlled.</li>
					<li>Thoughts mean you're doing it wrong.</li>
					<li>"Letting go," "non-attachment," a calm that can become dissociation.</li>
					<li>Meditation as retreat from ordinary life.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>

		<figure class="stance-quote">
			<blockquote>
				It wasn't until I realized how lonely and frustrating it was for my wife being married to
				the equanimous, distant version of Jared that I started to wonder if there was a different
				way to approach my meditation practice.
			</blockquote>
			<figcaption>— Jared Janes, cofounder of Evolving Ground</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.stance-section {
		background: var(--surface-elevated);
		padding: clamp(3.5rem, 5vw + 1rem, 6.5rem) 0;
	}

	.stance-heading {
		font-size: var(--fs-h2);
		font-weight: 390;
		letter-spacing: -0.018em;
		line-height: 1.12;
		margin: 0 0 clamp(1.5rem, 2vw + 0.5rem, 2.5rem);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	.stance-prose {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-sm);
	}

	.stance-prose p {
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--ink);
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* Spills a little past the text column, like the teacher photo, but never
	   pins to the viewport edge on wide windows. */
	.stance-collation {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 0 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
		max-width: 56rem;
		margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 3vw + 1rem, 4rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 2vw, 2.25rem);
		padding-right: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
	}

	.stance-col ul {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.85rem;
	}

	.stance-col li {
		font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
		font-weight: 400;
	}

	.stance-col + .stance-col {
		border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-left: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
	}

	.stance-col--this li {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 480;
	}

	.stance-quote {
		margin: clamp(3rem, 4vw + 1rem, 5rem) 0 0;
	}

	.stance-quote blockquote {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1rem + 1.2vw, 1.75rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.45;
		letter-spacing: -0.008em;
		color: var(--ink);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.stance-quote blockquote::before {
		content: '';
		display: block;
		width: 2.5rem;
		border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
		margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
	}

	.stance-quote figcaption {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--fs-metadata);
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		.stance-collation {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
			padding-right: 0;
		}

		.stance-col + .stance-col {
			border-left: 0;
			border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
			padding-left: 0;
			padding-top: 1.75rem;
		}
	}
</style>
